{
 "title": "A Fool's Mercy in 3D",
 "intro": "Moon Faire, in 3D. Two minutes in the night square with the camera close on the Jester: all ten of her moves against Envoi's lost souls, to Chris's songs Moonlit Forest Path and Herbal Decay. The square, its lights and every spell are built in code.",
 "footer": "<p>The square is built in code with three.js: every house, lamp, cobble and star, and every texture is painted on the fly. The Jester's frames come from the Flip Book Art export, drawn on their anchors on a card that turns to face the camera. The wisps, the Shadow Wraith and the great wraith are cut from Envoi's model and action sheets (envoi-on-the-longest-night). The music is Chris's Moonlit Forest Path and Herbal Decay (made with Suno, from follow-me-down-witch-way); the effects on top are synthesized in the browser, tuned to the songs.</p><p>Arrow keys skip 5 seconds. Space plays and pauses.</p>",
 "out": "dist/jester-square-3d.html",
